# "Another thread" has no spelling on the native backend: there is no `use c`
# yet, `std` has no concurrency, and the carrier threads native's own `ctl`
# mechanism runs on belong to the runtime rather than to the program
# (docs/oneshot-design.md 11.11). So the question is asked with `use java`,
# which the native backend refuses by design, and the native half of *this*
# question is `ctl_nested.drive` -- resumption from outside the frame that
# installed the handler, which native does run.
#
# run.sh still calls `__emitc` and fails if it succeeds, so this file cannot
# silence a program that does have a native half.
